cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the datalake it builds, please cite it as below."
title: "ste-enforcer"
abstract: >-
  A pre-commit/CI gate that detects violations of ASD-STE100 Simplified
  Technical English in prose files. Uses a hybrid detection approach: ~18
  mechanical violations (passive voice, long sentences, semicolons,
  contractions, nominalizations, marketing adjectives, phrasal verbs,
  banned synonyms, modal hedges, etc.) are caught by deterministic ONNX
  RegexFullMatch nodes (zero training data, verified 0 mismatches vs
  Python's re.search), and ~8 genuinely semantic violations by a SetFit
  few-shot classifier. Both branches plus a FLAN-T5 rewriter are exported
  to ONNX, backed by an Essential-Tuple-Normal-Form parquet+zstd datalake.
  NOT a certified ASD-STE100 checker. See https://asd-ste100.org for the
  complete specification.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/weftspun/tropes-removal-model"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-21"
keywords:
  - simplified-technical-english
  - asd-ste100
  - controlled-language
  - technical-writing
  - setfit
  - onnx
  - pre-commit
  - text-classification
references:
